.TH SOT "1" "2024\-2026" "sot" "Generated Python Manual"
.SH NAME
sot \- sot is a Command\-line System Observation Tool in the spirit of top. It displays various interesting system stats and graphs them. Works on all operating systems.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sot
[--help] [--version] [--log LOG] [--net NET] [--disk [DISK]] [--config-path] [--keys] [--theme THEME] {info,bench,disk,clean,ps} ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Command\-line System Obervation Tool ≈

.SH
POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fBsot\fR \fI\,info\/\fR
Print system information (the System view is key 4)
.TP
\fBsot\fR \fI\,bench\/\fR
Disk benchmarking view; flags run it without the TUI
.TP
\fBsot\fR \fI\,disk\/\fR
Disks view; \-\-list prints a table instead
.TP
\fBsot\fR \fI\,clean\/\fR
Clean caches, logs and temp files; \-\-dry\-run only reports
.TP
\fBsot\fR \fI\,ps\/\fR
Processes view: processes, listening ports, dev environments

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sot info'\/\fR
usage: sot info [\-h]

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sot bench'\/\fR
usage: sot bench [\-h] [\-\-output OUTPUT] [\-\-disk DISK] [\-\-duration DURATION]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sot bench'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI\,OUTPUT\/\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fI\,OUTPUT\/\fR
Output file for benchmark results (JSON format)

.TP
\fB\-\-disk\fR \fI\,DISK\/\fR
Disk to benchmark, by id (disk3, /dev/sda) or mountpoint; skips the prompt

.TP
\fB\-\-duration\fR \fI\,DURATION\/\fR, \fB\-d\fR \fI\,DURATION\/\fR
Duration for each benchmark test in seconds (default: 10s)

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sot disk'\/\fR
usage: sot disk [\-h] [\-\-list]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sot disk'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-list\fR, \fB\-l\fR
Print disks and partitions as a plain list instead of the TUI

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sot clean'\/\fR
usage: sot clean [\-h] [\-\-dry\-run]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sot clean'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be cleaned without actually deleting

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sot ps'\/\fR
usage: sot ps [\-h]

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR, \fB\-V\fR
Display version information with styling

.TP
\fB\-\-log\fR \fI\,LOG\/\fR, \fB\-L\fR \fI\,LOG\/\fR
Debug log file path (enables debug logging)

.TP
\fB\-\-net\fR \fI\,NET\/\fR, \fB\-N\fR \fI\,NET\/\fR
Network interface to display (default: auto\-detect best interface)

.TP
\fB\-\-disk\fR \fI\,[DISK]\/\fR, \fB\-D\fR \fI\,[DISK]\/\fR
Disk mountpoint to display (use without value for interactive selection)

.TP
\fB\-\-config\-path\fR
Print where sot reads its config file from

.TP
\fB\-\-keys\fR
List every key binding id, for the [keymap] config table

.TP
\fB\-\-theme\fR \fI\,THEME\/\fR, \fB\-T\fR \fI\,THEME\/\fR
Color theme: classic, cyberpunk (default: $SOT_THEME, config, or classic)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B sot
Launch the interactive system monitoring TUI
.TP
.B sot --net eth0
Monitor system with specific network interface
.TP
.B sot --disk
Pick the disk to monitor from a list
.TP
.B sot --disk /
Monitor system with root disk
.TP
.B sot --theme cyberpunk
Launch the TUI with the Cyberpunk 2077 inspired theme
.TP
.B sot info
Display comprehensive system information
.TP
.B sot bench
Open the Bench view: pick a disk, press Enter, export with e
.TP
.B sot bench --disk disk3 --duration 30 --output results.json
Run 30-second benchmarks without the TUI and save results to JSON
.TP
.B sot disk
Open the Disks view
.TP
.B sot disk --list
Print disks and partitions as a plain table and exit
.TP
.B sot clean --dry-run
Preview what would be cleaned without deleting
.TP
.B sot clean
Open the Clean view: pick targets, then c to clean after confirming
.TP
.B sot ps
Open the Processes view with ports and dev environments
.TP
.B sot --keys
List every key binding id for the [keymap] config table
.TP
.B sot --config-path
Show where the config file is read from

